  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I placed the contrast CT for Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015) and handled the RBC-RAD-07 prep, including sending him instructions.\n\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001), linked to his booked appointment on Mon 10/26 at 9:00 at St. Brigid Imaging (appt-t5-1026).\n- **Contrast allergy:** His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\" for iohexol (the CT dye). That label was added in 2021 from his own account, with no records checked. The radiology report from the day of the 2019 reaction describes hives and eyelid swelling with no breathing or blood-pressure problems, and grades it moderate. The policy says to grade by that same-day record, so this counts as moderate, not severe, and he can still have contrast with premedication. He was premedicated in 2023 with no reaction. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies don't count as risk factors.\n- **Premedication:**\n  - Prednisone 50 mg by mouth Sun 10/25 at 20:00, then Mon at 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0003).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth Mon at 08:00 (mr-t0004).\n  - He can't drive after the diphenhydramine and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney function:** He needs a recent creatinine because he's 64 and has diabetes. His 9/24 result came before an ER visit on 10/16–17 for dehydration with acute kidney injury. The ER creatinines (1.94, then 1.46 at discharge, not back to normal) were drawn during that injury, so they don't count. I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan, today through Mon 08:30 (sr-t0002). The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist will review the result that day.\n- **Metformin:** It's on hold because of the kidney injury. His last dose is Sunday evening, and it stays held for at least 48 hours after the scan. He restarts only once a recheck shows normal kidney function. That recheck creatinine is ordered for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006) and also covers the repeat kidney test the ER asked for. There's a task for you to review it and decide on restarting (task-t0009, due 10/30).\n- **Telling him what to do:** I sent him a portal message (comm-t0007) covering the blood test, the medication times, the driver, the metformin hold, possible higher blood sugar from the prednisone, fluids and reaction warning signs. I also asked the RN triage pool to call him today to confirm he got it (task-t0008).\n- **Chart note:** I wrote a progress note citing RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0010).\n\nDecision for you: I left the \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\" label on his allergy list as it is. You may want to correct it, since the 2019 report is the record of what actually happened.",
  "resumed": false,
